radv/android: report YUV AHB formats through u_gralloc (YV12, NV12, NV21)

RADV had its own vkGetAndroidHardwareBufferPropertiesANDROID that only
knew AHB formats with a fixed Vulkan equivalent and hardcoded BT.601 full
range. For YV12 (and NV21) it returned format = externalFormat = 0, so
ANGLE refused to create an EGLImage and SurfaceFlinger aborted on video
frames ("Failed to create a valid texture ... format:842094169").

Use the common implementation, which asks the gralloc (u_gralloc) for the
fourcc, plane layout and dataspace and reports external formats with
suggested YCbCr conversions. Teach it NV21 (NV12 layout, Cb/Cr swapped in
the conversion swizzle).

Also honour VkSamplerYcbcrConversionCreateInfo::components for external
formats (AHB apps pass samplerYcbcrConversionComponents there), which
is how NV21 gets its Cb/Cr swap.

